<title>MALAYSIA: MRCB, NST shares suspended.</title>
<headline>MRCB, NST shares suspended.</headline>
<dateline>KUALA LUMPUR 1996-09-10</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares of Malaysian Resources Corp Bhd (MRCB) and its 49 percent-owned associate, New Straits Times Press (Malaysia) Bhd (NST) were suspended on Tuesday at the request of the companies pending announcement, a Kuala Lumpur Stock Exchange official said.</p>
<p>Shares of MRCB, which is involved in media and communications, power generation and property and construction businesses, closed at 8.50 ringgit on Monday, and NST, a newspaper publisher, at 13.90 ringgit.</p>
<p>Officials of the companies could not be reached immediately for comment.</p>
</text>
